    {
      "id": "origin",
      "text": "The story starts in Atlanta in eighteen eighty-six, at a pharmacy soda fountain. Twenty years later, the first bottling plants outside the United States opened in three countries: Canada, Cuba and Panama. So how did one of the very first Coca-Cola countries end up without it?",
