    {
      "id": "cuba",
      "text": "Before the revolution, Coca-Cola was the island's favourite soft drink, from Havana to Santa Clara and Santiago de Cuba. But after nineteen fifty-nine, the new government nationalized private businesses, and Coca-Cola left. Then the United States placed a trade embargo on Cuba, and it is still in place today.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "chapter": "Country number one: Cuba",
        "view": {
          "lon": -79.3,
          "lat": 22.2,
