    {
      "id": "comebacks",
      "text": "Cuba is not the only country that lost its Coke. China went almost thirty years without it, until a deal in nineteen seventy-eight. India said goodbye in nineteen seventy-seven and welcomed it back in nineteen ninety-three. Vietnam got its first bottling plant in nineteen ninety-four. And Myanmar? Coke returned there in twenty twelve, after sixty years.",
      "scene": {
