    {
      "id": "scale",
      "text": "To see how rare this is, look at the scale. The Coca-Cola Company serves around two point two billion drinks every single day, in more than two hundred countries and territories. It owns thirty-two brands that each sell over a billion dollars a year. That is about one drink for every four people on the planet.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "bignum",
        "chapter": "A global giant",
        "value": 2.2,
        "fmt": "1dp",
        "suffix": " billion",
        "label": "drinks served every day",
        "note": "The Coca-Cola Company, investor relations",
        "chips": [
          "200+ countries",
          "32 billion-dollar brands"
        ],
        "cue": "two"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "russia",
      "text": "Country number three is the newest: Russia. Coca-Cola bottling began here in nineteen eighty-five, with drinks sold from Moscow to Saint Petersburg. Then, in March twenty twenty-two, after the war in Ukraine began, the company suspended its business. The former bottler now makes its own drink, called Dobry Cola.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "chapter": "Country number three: Russia",
        "view": {
